    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:569e72e117968fcc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "373a949a172334d58da7b187f8ab7b266ed13bc12027b1b61ad7a1de45be0830",
      "text": "6 February · Ascent to Corcovado by the open train through the Tijuca Forest, home to monkeys and exotic birds, to the statue of Christ the Redeemer (38 m), at about 710 m, inaugurated in 1931, with a breathtaking panorama of the Rio–Niterói Bridge, Guanabara Bay, the Botanical Garden, the Maracanã Stadium and Sugar Loaf. Lunch at Aprazível in Santa Teresa (not included), then the historic centre: the 18th-century Lapa Arches, the aqueduct that once carried water from the Carioca River, the Selarón Steps with their tiles from around the world, the Municipal Theatre, inspired by the Paris Opera, and the Metropolitan Cathedral. We recommend dinner at Marius Degustare (not included).\n\nEvening · The legendary Carnival Ball at the Copacabana Palace, from 22:00 to 05:00: an exclusive night of elegance, haute cuisine and impeccable service.",
      "provenance": {
